CORD instrumentation for case R2 (cFE #2663) on cFS v7.0.1 (bundle 088b2fa8, cFE c5fb2b4d)
==========================================================================================
Date: 2026-10-08. Applies with `patch -p1` in the cFS bundle root. "a/" = the ENV source tree
(/home/user/work/procrace/cfs_ref/cFS without .git and build-native_std); "b/" = the instrumented copy
(/home/user/work/procrace/cfs_cord/cFS). The copy equalled the ENV source before patching
(env/logs/cord_build_00_copy_manifest.txt). This diff is the complete difference between the two trees
(`diff -ruN --exclude=.git --exclude=build-native_std`): 14 files, 2 of them new.
Event model: tool/DESIGN.md; recorder: tool/cord/cord.{c,h} (copied verbatim to cfe/cord/, same sha256:
cord.c f1f6780d..., cord.h 290499e3...). Without -DCORD_ENABLE every added statement compiles to nothing.

Build integration (cfe/modules/{es,sb,evs}/CMakeLists.txt)
  - cord.c is added to the `es` static library only (target_sources), compiled with the target's own flags
    plus "-std=c11" (cord.c uses C11 _Atomic; with the build's -std=c99 -pedantic -Werror it does not compile).
